  The draft says the petition was submitted to the 'ஆட்சியர் அலுவலகம்' (Collector's office) in Salem; the article says 'கலெக்டர் அலுவலகம', which is the same, so this is fine, but the reel_script says 'சேலம் ஆட்சியர் அலுவலகத்தில்' correctly — no issue there.
  The reel_script says 'இரு நீதிபதிகள் அமரும் தீபம் ஏற்ற உத்தரவிட்டது' — this is ungrammatical and garbled: 'அமரும்' (sitting) makes no sense; it should say the two-judge bench ordered the lamp to be lit.
  The reel_script and caption say the 2025 High Court order was issued by the 'உயர்நீதிமன்ற மதுரை கிளை' and the draft mixes that order with the 2025 date in a single sentence while the article says the DMK government 'உதாசீனப்படுத்தி' (disregarded) it and appealed; the draft's reel_script instead says 'முந்தைய தி மு க அரசு பின்பற்றவில்லை' which is roughly accurate, but the appeal against the order (மேல்முறையீடு) and the claim that devotees were insulted are missing from the reel_script — an important fact of the article omitted.
  The caption claims the petition was submitted 'நேற்று' and the footer date is 'நவம்பர் 17, 2026 (நேற்று மனு அளிக்கப்பட்டது)' — the footer date is excluded from checking, but the claim 'நேற்று' matches the article, so no issue.
  The reel_script states the court order was issued 'in 2025' and that the DMK government 'தடுத்ததாக' prevented the lighting, while the article says the DMK government 'தடுத்துவிட்டது' after the two-judge bench order — the sequence is preserved, so this is acceptable.
  The slides_spec 'cat' field labels the story 'கோயில் செய்தி' and 'hl1' says 'ஆட்சியர் அலுவலகம்: தீபம் ஏற்ற மனு' — no factual conflict with the article.
